# A readable name for the route table mango-vpnguard builds.
#
# Cosmetic only. The helper always addresses the table by its number, so a
# missing or ignored name can never break the guard — it only makes
# `ip route show table direct` easier to read at 3am than
# `ip route show table 1001`.
#
# `ip` merges every *.conf in this directory with the packaged
# /usr/share/iproute2/rt_tables, so this adds a name without editing a file
# pacman owns.
#
# 1001  direct   a default route via the physical uplink's own gateway.
#                Packets the ruleset's `marks` chain stamps 0x1 are sent
#                here instead of down the tunnel's default route.
1001	direct
